Advanced Options

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:20.000
<i>I have to make a decision 
about what comes next.</i>

00:03:23.050 --> 00:03:24.890
Souta-san, welcome back!

00:03:25.270 --> 00:03:26.750
We've been waiting for you!

00:03:26.750 --> 00:03:28.820
Now we should be able to weather the storm.

00:03:28.820 --> 00:03:30.020
This is great.

00:03:30.470 --> 00:03:32.410
By the way, who's the kid?

00:03:32.710 --> 00:03:34.900
Oh, well, that's a long story.

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:37.480
So cute!

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:39.030
He hid!

00:03:40.660 --> 00:03:43.780
I'm so sorry. It was one thing after another...

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:45.550
This is a souvenir from Kagawa.

00:03:45.550 --> 00:03:47.180
Oh! A souvenir?

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:48.180
<b>Kamado</b>

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:52.470
Mikko-chan, is the reception 
room in use today?

00:03:52.470 --> 00:03:56.020
Oh, right. The development team was 
up all night trying to hit deadlines.

00:03:56.020 --> 00:03:57.250
They're all dead.

00:03:57.250 --> 00:03:59.030
Ah... I thought so.

00:04:00.630 --> 00:04:01.530
Tawara.

00:04:03.330 --> 00:04:04.640
Come with me.

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:06.230
Yes, sir.

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:08.070
Poco, wait here, okay?

00:04:08.070 --> 00:04:09.390
I'll be right back.

00:04:09.820 --> 00:04:11.770
Souta! Souta!

00:04:12.140 --> 00:04:16.080
Souta-kun has to talk with the 
scary old man, so stay here, okay?

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:17.650
You must be hot in that hood.

00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:18.770
Let's take that off.

00:04:19.990 --> 00:04:22.570
Poco, leave your hood up, okay?

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:25.530
Ah, he ran!

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:25.910
No, no!

00:04:26.420 --> 00:04:28.530
Souta!

00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:52.060
<b>In Use</b>

00:04:49.770 --> 00:04:52.060
You want to extend your vacation?

00:04:52.370 --> 00:04:53.300
Yes, sir.

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:56.100
What are you trying to do?

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:58.520
It's exactly as I just explained, sir.

00:04:58.820 --> 00:05:00.790
I can't just abandon Poco—

00:05:00.790 --> 00:05:01.690
I don't get it.

00:05:01.690 --> 00:05:02.940
I don't get it at all!

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:05.350
I realize that you must have a lot going

00:05:05.350 --> 00:05:07.870
through your mind after your father's death.

00:05:08.230 --> 00:05:12.190
What I don't understand is why 
you have to take in a friend's kid!

00:05:12.490 --> 00:05:15.430
Even so, it's just, well...

00:05:15.430 --> 00:05:17.380
Something I feel I have to do.

00:05:17.380 --> 00:05:19.400
Just how delicate of a heart do you have?

00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:21.840
Are you naïve? Are you a vegetable? Huh?

00:05:25.870 --> 00:05:28.450
What do you plan on doing with the kid?

00:05:28.450 --> 00:05:30.790
Like I said, at least for now, 
he'll live with me—

00:05:30.790 --> 00:05:34.570
Caring for a kid isn't the same as 
keeping a dog or cat, you know.

00:05:34.570 --> 00:05:36.230
What's more, it's not even your kid.

00:05:36.230 --> 00:05:37.530
And they're expensive, too.

00:05:38.260 --> 00:05:39.100
Yes, sir.

00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:42.940
I need you.

00:05:42.940 --> 00:05:44.890
The other members feel the same way.

00:05:45.540 --> 00:05:48.560
Over the last ten years, 
you've done great work.

00:05:49.340 --> 00:05:53.200
And you're a creator at heart, aren't you?

00:05:55.030 --> 00:05:58.920
What's changed since you decided 
to come to Tokyo after high school?

00:06:02.190 --> 00:06:03.330
Souta-san!

00:06:04.310 --> 00:06:06.730
Welcome back, Souta-san!

00:06:05.990 --> 00:06:07.050
Souta!

00:06:07.050 --> 00:06:08.210
Hiroshi!

00:06:08.210 --> 00:06:09.890
What's with the kid?

00:06:09.890 --> 00:06:11.550
Hiroshi, put him down.

00:06:10.110 --> 00:06:11.550
Souta!

00:06:12.020 --> 00:06:15.690
Oh my God! Is he yours?

00:06:15.540 --> 00:06:18.560
Souta! Souta!

00:06:15.690 --> 00:06:17.740
An accident? A surprise kid?

00:06:18.560 --> 00:06:20.810
Argh! Quiet down!

00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:24.060
This isn't a nursery school! Enough!

00:06:24.060 --> 00:06:24.680
He's a gorilla.

00:06:24.680 --> 00:06:25.570
A gorilla...

00:06:25.940 --> 00:06:29.010
Hey, so what were you two 
talking about in here, anyway?

00:06:29.010 --> 00:06:31.570
Oh, uh... Actually...

00:06:31.810 --> 00:06:34.850
He says he wants to take some 
time off to look after the kid.

00:06:34.850 --> 00:06:35.580
Huh?

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:37.200
No way!

00:06:37.470 --> 00:06:41.430
But Souta-san came back when I called him.

00:06:41.430 --> 00:06:43.420
There's no way that's true.

00:06:43.420 --> 00:06:44.340
Right, Souta-san?

00:06:45.470 --> 00:06:46.910
I'm sorry, Hiroshi.

00:06:46.910 --> 00:06:49.470
I can't come back to work yet.

00:06:50.760 --> 00:06:52.470
What do you mean?

00:06:52.970 --> 00:06:55.130
Souta-san, didn't you come back to work on

00:06:55.130 --> 00:06:57.450
the project you're teamed up with me on?

00:06:57.750 --> 00:06:59.600
My situation's changed.

00:07:01.430 --> 00:07:02.590
What are you saying?

00:07:04.570 --> 00:07:06.530
Is it because of this kid? 
Is it your fault?

00:07:08.670 --> 00:07:10.610
Souta...

00:07:12.510 --> 00:07:14.700
I'm gonna go toss him in the Sumida River!

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:16.680
Hiroshi, stop it!

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:26.170
It was just a joke.

00:07:28.400 --> 00:07:31.730
Well, just think it over one more time.

00:07:45.980 --> 00:07:47.230
Hamada-san!

00:07:48.050 --> 00:07:51.610
Thank you so much for everything 
you taught me about home pages.

00:07:52.160 --> 00:07:54.010
Is that counter going up?

00:07:54.010 --> 00:07:54.900
Yes!

00:07:54.900 --> 00:07:57.130
And today, we got our first...

00:07:57.130 --> 00:07:58.370
We got our first comment!

00:07:58.370 --> 00:07:59.240
Oh?

00:07:59.530 --> 00:08:03.000
We'd been putting up the fishing spot 
along with the fish rubbings.

00:08:03.300 --> 00:08:06.750
The commenter said they'd try fishing 
at the same spot sometime, and...

00:08:06.750 --> 00:08:08.750
They said the home page was easy to read.

00:08:09.120 --> 00:08:10.560
That's great.

00:08:10.560 --> 00:08:11.350
Yeah!

00:08:11.350 --> 00:08:13.970
I never knew that other people

00:08:14.270 --> 00:08:18.510
could find joy in something that I created.

00:08:18.990 --> 00:08:20.810
I'm really happy about it!

00:08:22.750 --> 00:08:24.560
I'm sure you are.

00:08:25.030 --> 00:08:26.650
When your leg's better,

00:08:26.650 --> 00:08:28.250
you should visit Tokyo sometime.

00:08:29.660 --> 00:08:31.320
I'll show you around.

00:08:33.530 --> 00:08:34.450
I will!

00:08:34.450 --> 00:08:37.640
Next time we meet, you can call me "Dahama."

00:08:37.640 --> 00:08:40.800
Cool! Like an industry name!

00:08:43.690 --> 00:08:44.340
Tawara.

00:08:44.340 --> 00:08:45.460
Yes, sir?

00:08:46.200 --> 00:08:47.580
Go home for the day.

00:08:47.900 --> 00:08:49.270
But I'm still not...

00:08:49.270 --> 00:08:52.050
I want to at least finish 
everything that's on a deadline.

00:08:52.050 --> 00:08:55.340
I don't mean you. The kid's had enough.

00:08:56.030 --> 00:08:58.190
Think of how the kid must feel,

00:08:58.190 --> 00:09:00.320
being dragged around at your convenience.

00:09:02.750 --> 00:09:03.890
Thank you.

00:09:04.220 --> 00:09:05.220
I'll go home.

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:14.740
What's wrong? You're not going to eat?

00:09:16.560 --> 00:09:18.110
You look pale.

00:09:18.110 --> 00:09:19.150
Are you okay?

00:09:19.530 --> 00:09:21.620
You didn't eat lunch today, either.

00:09:32.580 --> 00:09:34.510
Poco, use your fork to—

00:09:40.290 --> 00:09:42.930
Excuse me! Check, please!

00:09:44.980 --> 00:09:46.810
Poco, are you okay?

00:09:47.610 --> 00:09:50.010
Think of how the kid must feel,

00:09:50.010 --> 00:09:52.200
being dragged around at your convenience.

00:09:52.680 --> 00:09:53.670
I'm sorry.

00:09:53.670 --> 00:09:55.490
I'll go draw the bath.

00:09:55.490 --> 00:09:57.070
We'll go to bed early.

00:10:05.210 --> 00:10:06.140
Poco!

00:10:07.870 --> 00:10:09.830
Poco... Poco!

00:10:15.570 --> 00:10:16.580
He's burning up...

00:10:16.580 --> 00:10:17.630
The hospital!

00:10:17.970 --> 00:10:19.380
No, we can't...

00:10:19.380 --> 00:10:21.270
If they see him like this...

00:10:21.270 --> 00:10:22.530
Oh, yeah! Nakajima!

00:10:22.530 --> 00:10:23.750
Nakajima will know what to do!

00:10:30.290 --> 00:10:32.790
The customer you have called is not available.

00:10:32.790 --> 00:10:37.390
Please leave a message after the tone.

00:10:34.080 --> 00:10:36.320
<i>Stay calm. Stay calm...</i>

00:10:37.240 --> 00:10:38.350
<i>What do I do?</i>

00:10:38.660 --> 00:10:39.720
<i>What can I...</i>

00:10:41.760 --> 00:10:43.170
Souta...

00:10:47.550 --> 00:10:50.580
<i>Poco doesn't have anyone but me!</i>

00:10:53.910 --> 00:10:56.010
Hiroshi, for the love of...

00:10:56.520 --> 00:10:57.470
What are these?

00:10:58.360 --> 00:10:59.510
Marshmallows?

00:10:59.510 --> 00:11:02.010
Dahama-san, where did Souta-san go?

00:11:02.630 --> 00:11:04.310
I sent him home.

00:11:04.310 --> 00:11:06.600
The kid didn't look well.

00:11:06.880 --> 00:11:08.750
Huh? The kid?

00:11:10.420 --> 00:11:11.600
Say "ah."

00:11:14.960 --> 00:11:16.860
There you go. Just a little at a time.

00:11:17.810 --> 00:11:19.850
Seems like you're a little dehydrated.

00:11:20.270 --> 00:11:22.980
You didn't eat or drink anything all day...

00:11:22.980 --> 00:11:24.410
Were you nervous?

00:11:25.310 --> 00:11:25.880
Huh?

00:11:26.890 --> 00:11:27.700
Hello?

00:11:28.200 --> 00:11:29.500
Souta-san!

00:11:29.500 --> 00:11:30.360
Hiroshi?!

00:11:30.360 --> 00:11:31.600
Wait... What? What? What?!

00:11:31.600 --> 00:11:33.190
Please just let me in!

00:11:33.190 --> 00:11:34.670
No, no, no! You can't right now!

00:11:34.670 --> 00:11:36.310
He's been sick, and he's sleeping!

00:11:36.310 --> 00:11:39.430
Come on! Let me see him just for a minute!

00:11:39.730 --> 00:11:42.350
<i>If I let him in, he'll see Poco's ears and tail!</i>

00:11:42.350 --> 00:11:45.690
Just for a minute! It's just for a minute!

00:11:44.720 --> 00:11:45.880
Give it a rest!

00:11:45.880 --> 00:11:47.260
Seriously, what's with you?

00:11:50.050 --> 00:11:53.410
I... I came to apologize to the kid.

00:11:54.400 --> 00:11:56.610
But I'm not going to apologize to you!

00:11:56.610 --> 00:11:57.870
Wait! Stop!

00:11:57.870 --> 00:11:58.150
Kid!

00:11:58.610 --> 00:11:59.700
Sorry about today!

00:11:59.700 --> 00:12:01.150
I brought this to make it up to...

00:12:01.150 --> 00:12:01.810
you?

00:12:08.540 --> 00:12:10.010
<i>It's over!</i>

00:12:15.460 --> 00:12:17.570
Er...

00:12:17.870 --> 00:12:20.010
Oh! I know, I know! It's... that!

00:12:20.010 --> 00:12:24.300
Those trendy animal ear headphones 
that move because of brain waves!

00:12:24.300 --> 00:12:26.710
But doesn't that toy

00:12:26.710 --> 00:12:28.750
have cat ears?

00:12:30.050 --> 00:12:30.840
Huh?

00:12:31.460 --> 00:12:32.660
That's strange.

00:12:32.660 --> 00:12:33.660
It's not coming off.

00:12:33.960 --> 00:12:35.140
Why not?

00:12:35.140 --> 00:12:37.300
It's almost like... like...

00:12:37.740 --> 00:12:39.320
Are these his real ears?

00:12:42.740 --> 00:12:43.750
There are no ears.

00:12:44.380 --> 00:12:45.950
Huh? Uh, but...

00:12:46.170 --> 00:12:47.400
There are no ears!

00:12:51.420 --> 00:12:52.960
Go to sleep.

00:12:52.960 --> 00:12:54.540
You're tired from working so late.

00:12:54.540 --> 00:12:56.610
Here, put this on.

00:12:56.930 --> 00:12:58.220
Huh? What's going on?

00:12:58.220 --> 00:13:00.030
It's dark! I'm scared!

00:13:00.030 --> 00:13:02.120
I don't like this!

00:13:11.620 --> 00:13:13.090
<i>He saw everything!</i>

00:13:13.090 --> 00:13:15.670
<i>What am I gonna do? 
What the heck am I gonna do?</i>

00:13:17.230 --> 00:13:20.190
<i>No! I can't go freaking out when Poco needs me.</i>

00:13:28.840 --> 00:13:31.740
<i>I have to protect Poco's secret,</i>

00:13:32.140 --> 00:13:33.520
<i>and Poco himself, too.</i>

00:13:50.210 --> 00:13:51.140
Souta!

00:13:52.970 --> 00:13:53.840
Poco!

00:13:54.430 --> 00:13:56.210
You feel well enough to be up?

00:13:56.210 --> 00:13:56.790
Uh-huh.

00:13:57.150 --> 00:13:58.540
Souta, udon!

00:13:58.540 --> 00:13:58.940
Huh?

00:13:59.360 --> 00:14:00.320
Udon!

00:14:00.560 --> 00:14:03.500
Oh... You want to eat udon?

00:14:03.500 --> 00:14:04.180
Uh-huh!

00:14:04.070 --> 00:14:05.820
<b>Gurgle</b>

00:14:04.650 --> 00:14:05.820
<b>Rumble</b>

00:14:06.070 --> 00:14:07.240
Poltergeist?!

00:14:07.240 --> 00:14:07.700
Huh?

00:14:09.520 --> 00:14:11.610
Souta-san, please step aside!

00:14:11.610 --> 00:14:12.960
Wh-What is it?

00:14:12.960 --> 00:14:15.750
Hiroshi, you've been acting 
kinda strange since yesterday!

00:14:19.790 --> 00:14:21.830
Huh?

00:14:32.660 --> 00:14:33.680
Yummy.

00:14:34.600 --> 00:14:36.340
I know he had them...

00:14:36.340 --> 00:14:38.910
Ears and a tail! They even felt soft!

00:14:38.910 --> 00:14:40.810
What are you talking about? 
You're imagining things.

00:14:41.100 --> 00:14:42.600
But he's...

00:14:42.600 --> 00:14:45.060
Wow! This udon is delicious!

00:14:45.060 --> 00:14:46.190
Where did you buy it?

00:14:46.470 --> 00:14:49.790
Some of these Kagawa products 
are ones I've never seen...

00:14:49.790 --> 00:14:53.690
Oh, right. Yesterday, I bought all this 
at a specialty shop for Kagawa products.

00:14:56.080 --> 00:14:57.610
Something wrong?

00:14:59.100 --> 00:15:00.720
Hiroshi, I'm sorry.

00:15:01.110 --> 00:15:02.960
I'm going back to Kagawa, after all.

00:15:04.530 --> 00:15:05.740
You made up your mind?

00:15:06.040 --> 00:15:06.730
Yeah.

00:15:07.980 --> 00:15:10.590
Oh... So you're going back...

00:15:11.160 --> 00:15:13.880
Dahama-san will be disappointed.

00:15:13.880 --> 00:15:16.470
He had high hopes for you.

00:15:17.140 --> 00:15:19.480
Sorry. But I've made up my mind.

00:15:19.780 --> 00:15:21.230
Yeah...

00:15:21.580 --> 00:15:23.720
You can't abandon him.

00:15:24.710 --> 00:15:28.720
I wonder who'll replace you on our project.

00:15:29.210 --> 00:15:30.020
Hiroshi.

00:15:30.420 --> 00:15:30.990
Yes?

00:15:31.760 --> 00:15:33.890
Dahama-san can be intimidating,

00:15:33.890 --> 00:15:36.740
but if you do good work, 
he will acknowledge it.

00:15:37.400 --> 00:15:40.070
That's the kind of person our boss is.

00:15:42.160 --> 00:15:44.630
But I... I really did want to do

00:15:44.630 --> 00:15:46.750
this current project with you.

00:15:50.640 --> 00:15:52.330
Thanks for the food.

00:15:58.710 --> 00:16:01.060
Oh, crap! It's already this late?!

00:16:01.060 --> 00:16:03.400
No way! We have to get to the office!

00:16:05.210 --> 00:16:06.320
Tawara.

00:16:06.990 --> 00:16:08.150
Tawara!

00:16:08.990 --> 00:16:09.650
Huh?

00:16:10.780 --> 00:16:12.550
A-hup...

00:16:13.040 --> 00:16:15.720
That looks good. Did Tawara make it?

00:16:15.720 --> 00:16:17.510
Rice ball!

00:16:17.510 --> 00:16:19.470
Oh? I can have it?

00:16:23.280 --> 00:16:24.660
That's yummy.

00:16:24.660 --> 00:16:25.740
Yummy, yummy!

00:16:27.100 --> 00:16:30.190
<i>He's good with his hands...</i>

00:16:30.810 --> 00:16:32.470
Oh, Dahama-san.

00:16:33.090 --> 00:16:35.230
Uh... What are you doing?

00:16:35.230 --> 00:16:36.990
I was looking for you, Tawara.

00:16:36.990 --> 00:16:38.720
The kid looks better.

00:16:38.720 --> 00:16:41.050
Yeah. Thanks again.

00:16:41.050 --> 00:16:42.480
That's great.

00:16:42.970 --> 00:16:45.780
Now, about what we discussed yesterday...

00:16:46.100 --> 00:16:48.610
I know what I said, but, well...

00:16:49.510 --> 00:16:51.260
If you do end up taking time off,

00:16:51.260 --> 00:16:53.460
just make sure you pass along the baton right.

00:16:55.690 --> 00:16:57.870
Actually, about that...

00:17:01.000 --> 00:17:02.790
<b>Resignation</b>

00:17:01.800 --> 00:17:04.500
Please accept my resignation.

00:17:06.500 --> 00:17:07.430
And...

00:17:07.830 --> 00:17:10.130
I know I'm in no position to ask this, but...

00:17:10.480 --> 00:17:12.700
Will you allow me

00:17:12.700 --> 00:17:14.760
to complete the project with Hiroshi?

00:17:15.460 --> 00:17:17.270
I promise we'll make something good.

00:17:22.140 --> 00:17:23.320
Please!

00:17:34.040 --> 00:17:36.360
You're as clumsy as ever.

00:17:36.530 --> 00:17:38.370
<b>Resignation</b>

00:17:37.110 --> 00:17:38.370
I'll keep this.

00:17:38.660 --> 00:17:41.660
Call Hiroshi. We're going to 
scout locations this afternoon.

00:17:41.660 --> 00:17:42.750
Yes, sir!

00:17:43.360 --> 00:17:44.850
Thank you!

00:17:56.920 --> 00:17:57.960
Poco!

00:17:57.960 --> 00:17:59.850
Bouncing won't help you reach it.

00:17:59.850 --> 00:18:02.140
We're about to climb that!

00:18:26.670 --> 00:18:27.470
Tawara...

00:18:27.770 --> 00:18:28.430
Yes?

00:18:29.150 --> 00:18:31.170
When you get back to Kagawa, 
if you have the time,

00:18:31.170 --> 00:18:32.780
you should visit Shodoshima.

00:18:33.100 --> 00:18:34.250
Shodoshima?

00:18:34.550 --> 00:18:37.700
A friend of mine runs an 
advertising agency there.

00:18:38.100 --> 00:18:41.600
It's called Team Planet. 
They do some Web work, too.

00:18:41.600 --> 00:18:44.440
Really? There's a company 
like that on Shodoshima?

00:18:44.850 --> 00:18:48.320
He can be a disagreeable guy, 
but he's good at his job.

00:18:48.320 --> 00:18:50.260
Meeting him might

00:18:50.260 --> 00:18:52.900
help give you some perspective.

00:18:53.740 --> 00:18:55.150
Dahama-san...

00:18:56.920 --> 00:18:58.410
Thank you.

00:18:58.760 --> 00:19:02.510
I'm glad the company I had the opportunity 
to work for in Tokyo was yours.

00:19:06.110 --> 00:19:07.860
What's up? What are you talking about?

00:19:08.460 --> 00:19:09.400
We're leaving.

00:19:09.400 --> 00:19:10.790
Wait... What?

00:19:11.210 --> 00:19:14.020
Dahama-san! Wait!

00:19:25.930 --> 00:19:27.650
Scratchy, scratchy...

00:19:28.450 --> 00:19:29.510
Souta-san.

00:19:29.510 --> 00:19:31.560
Can I visit you in Kagawa sometime?

00:19:32.210 --> 00:19:33.110
Sure.

00:19:33.110 --> 00:19:34.190
Awesome!

00:19:45.700 --> 00:19:47.790
<i>He did have them, right?</i>

00:19:47.790 --> 00:19:49.200
<i>Ears and a tail...</i>

00:19:49.510 --> 00:19:50.910
Hiroshi? What is it?

00:19:50.910 --> 00:19:52.960
Ah, nothing!

00:19:53.440 --> 00:19:56.050
How long do you think 
it takes to bike to Kagawa?

00:19:56.050 --> 00:19:58.090
Huh? You're coming on a bike?!

00:21:32.310 --> 00:21:37.980
<b>Gaogao-chan and</b>

00:21:34.890 --> 00:21:37.980
<b>The Blue Sky</b>

00:21:38.710 --> 00:21:42.600
<i>The Tale of Gaogao-chan and the Resignation!</i>

00:21:38.730 --> 00:21:43.990
<b>Episode 6: 
"Gaogao-chan and the Resignation!"</b>

00:21:46.430 --> 00:21:49.120
<i>Gaogao-chan left on a journey in secret.</i>

00:21:49.120 --> 00:21:50.620
<b>I went out to play. 
I'll be back by dinner.
From Gaogao</b>

00:21:49.780 --> 00:21:51.120
<i>Gaogao-chan wanted</i>

00:21:51.120 --> 00:21:53.980
<i>to take responsibility as a man.</i>

00:21:54.460 --> 00:21:56.330
<b>Resignation</b>

00:21:56.940 --> 00:21:58.580
<i>I don't understand at all, Gao!</i>

00:21:59.090 --> 00:22:00.710
<i>Even so,</i>

00:22:00.710 --> 00:22:03.340
<i>it's just something I feel I have to do...</i>

00:22:03.630 --> 00:22:05.220
<i>Fool!</i>

00:22:05.220 --> 00:22:07.340
<i>But Papa, on Earth...</i>

00:22:08.930 --> 00:22:12.930
<i>There were so many beautiful, warm,</i>

00:22:13.360 --> 00:22:17.690
<i>and moving things, Gao!</i>

00:22:22.380 --> 00:22:24.120
<i>Do what you want, Gao.</i>

00:22:25.540 --> 00:22:27.910
<i>Thank you for everything, Gao.</i>

00:22:30.110 --> 00:22:32.470
<i>Do good work, even on Earth, Gao.</i>

00:22:32.840 --> 00:22:35.440
<i>Don't go soft, Gao!</i>

00:22:35.950 --> 00:22:40.960
